    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to present 185 St Attracta Road to the market. This charming two-bedroom mid-terrace home has been thoughtfully extended to the rear and offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation extending to approximately 67 sq.m. Beautifully presented throughout, the property combines period character with a warm contemporary style, featuring a spacious open-plan living room and kitchen, a separate dining room extension, two generous double bedrooms and a modern shower room. The home has been significantly upgraded in recent years with rewiring, a Worcester gas combi boiler, A-rated windows and doors throughout and a high-quality composite front door. One of its most appealing features is the abundance of natural light that fills the house throughout the day, creating a bright, warm and welcoming atmosphere. Complementing the interior is a wonderful mature rear garden, thoughtfully designed using organic and pollinator-friendly principles, providing a peaceful retreat rarely found so close to the city centre. Situated on the ever-popular St Attracta Road, this is an ideal home for first-time buyers, downsizers and those seeking a well-connected Dublin 7 address.\n\nEntering the home, the entrance hall leads through to a bright and welcoming living room where a marble fireplace forms an attractive focal point. Large windows flood the space with natural light, while the open-plan connection to the kitchen creates a sociable and practical layout for modern living.\n\nThe kitchen is fitted with bespoke timber units and generous worktop space, complemented by a breakfast bar and attractive tiled splashback. Beyond, a dining room extension overlooks the rear garden and provides an ideal space for everyday dining and entertaining.\n\nUpstairs, there are two spacious double bedrooms. The principal bedroom spans almost the full width of the house and benefits from original timber flooring, fitted storage and triple-glazed windows. The second bedroom is equally well presented and enjoys a peaceful outlook over the rear garden.\n\nCompleting the accommodation is a bright contemporary shower room finished with modern tiling and a large walk-in shower.\n\nTo the rear lies a truly special garden. Lovingly designed and maintained using organic growing and pollinator-friendly principles, the garden provides a peaceful oasis filled with mature planting, fruit trees, flowering shrubs and culinary herbs. Meandering pathways lead through richly planted borders to a greenhouse at the rear, creating an attractive and productive outdoor space that can be enjoyed throughout the year. The garden's thoughtful design, biodiversity and sense of tranquillity make it a genuine extension of the living accommodation.\n\nSt Attracta Road is one of Cabra's most established and convenient residential locations. Ideally positioned close to local shops, schools, parks and sporting facilities, the area also benefits from excellent public transport links, including nearby bus routes and the Luas at Cabra. The Phoenix Park, TUD Grangegorman, Phibsborough Village and Dublin City Centre are all easily accessible, making this a highly desirable location for those seeking the perfect balance between city living and a strong community atmosphere"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nA welcoming entrance hall providing access to the main living accommodation.\n\nLiving Room (4.90m x 3.30m) - \nA bright reception room featuring a marble fireplace and excellent natural light from the front-facing window. Open plan to the kitchen, creating a spacious and sociable living area.\n\nKitchen (2.20m x 4.30m) - \nFitted with attractive timber units, generous worktop space, breakfast bar seating and a stylish tiled splashback.\n\nDining Room (3.50m x 2.00m) - \nA bright rear extension overlooking the garden, providing an ideal setting for dining and entertaining.\n\nShower Room (1.80m x 2.00m) - \nModern shower room fitted with a walk-in shower, WC and wash hand basin, finished with contemporary tiling.\n\nBedroom 1 (3.35m x 4.30m) - \nA spacious double bedroom spanning almost the full width of the house, featuring original timber flooring, fitted storage and triple-glazed windows.\n\nBedroom 2 (3.17m x 4.30m) - \nA generous double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, enjoying excellent natural light and a peaceful outlook.\n\nRear Garden - \nA beautifully maintained mature garden designed using organic and pollinator-friendly principles. The garden features extensive planting, productive growing areas, fruit trees, mature shrubs and a greenhouse, creating a wonderful outdoor retreat.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
